I disagree on that. I usually have no big trouble letting my large cat/dog  
kill the first unicorn I met and I'm even glad to let it eat the corpse to  
get hand on the horn...
At that time, I usually have not identified lots of potion (except  
price-id) and #dip the horn in all of them. In almost every game I end up  
naming several potion "100$ - danger" because I don't know more after  
dipping the horn (and don't need to know more until I happen to get full  
ID from a scroll).
And I always find swimming boring because it takes lots of time to remove  
and drop everything, go swim, find out that I was too lucky and nothing is  
blanked, and repeat. If I can grab enough harmful potions to have enough  
water just with the horn, I'm quite happy.

Well, I guess your mileage may vary, of course, but I find the horn/potion  
interaction really useful at the time I met unicorns.

The fatc the the horn is guaranteed is indeed consistant with the nature  
of the beast, but not really with the fact that dragon scales are not  
guaranteed death drop.

